  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound (4aR,5aS,8aR,15bR)-10,11-dimethoxy-4a,5,5a,7,8,13a,15,15a,15b,16-decahydro-2H-4,6-methanoindolo[3,2,1-ij]oxepino[2,3,4-de]pyrrolo[2,3-h]quinoline-14-one and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, as it is identified as a target of multiple compounds that interact with this complex. Specifically, the compound is a target of Phakellistatin 15 and of 5,7-dihydroxy-2-(4-hydroxy-3-methoxyphenyl)-3-[(2S,4R,5S)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-[[(2R,4R,5R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-methyloxan-2-yl]oxymethyl]oxan-2-yl]oxychromen-4-one, which itself is a target of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. Additionally, the compound is also a target of 5,7,3',4',5'-Pentahydroxy-3,6,8-trimethoxyflavone, which is also a target of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These findings suggest that the compound may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a mechanism involving its ability to modulate the activity of the complex, potentially through binding or other molecular interactions. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, indicating a possible role for the compound in influencing the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex.",
